   "insight": {
    "headline": "IT is being repriced, not just sold",
    "body": "Only 12 of 44 large caps rose, and IT was the epicentre for a third straight session - Infosys down 4.84%, HCL Tech 4.44%, dragging the sector average to -3.17%. Industrials were the sole sector in the green at +0.79%. The Nifty lost 0.95% to 24,203 and Bank Nifty fell harder at -1.04%. The rupee slid again to 95.66. Three sessions with the same sector at the bottom is not sentiment, it is repricing - and the reason is visible in the US board, where semiconductors gained 4.62% while broader technology fell 3.38%. Money is moving toward the firms selling AI hardware and away from those selling software services. Indian IT sits in the second group."
