   "insight": {
    "headline": "Semiconductors and software went opposite ways",
    "body": "The headline indices barely moved - S&P down 0.10%, Nasdaq up 0.15% - but underneath was one of the sharpest sector splits in weeks. Semiconductors rose 4.62% on average while technology fell 3.38%, with Cerebras up 15.07% and AXT 17.55%. Energy gained 2.52% as crude spiked. The Dow's 0.96% fall against a flat Nasdaq says old-economy industrials lagged. This is the Nvidia-backstop story showing up in prices: capital is flowing to whoever sells the picks and shovels of AI infrastructure, and away from the software firms expected to pay for them."
   }
