   "insight": {
    "headline": "Hong Kong tech took another beating",
    "body": "The split between the mainland and Hong Kong widened again. Shenzhen rose 0.69% and Shanghai 0.46%, while the Hang Seng fell 1.44%. Technology was the cause for a second day: Meituan down 9.30%, Tencent 6.88%, Xiaomi 4.35%, taking the sector average to -5.63%. What rose were the state-linked financials - AgBank +1.40%, ICBC +1.06%. Two consecutive sessions of heavy selling in the same four Hong Kong-listed names, with mainland boards firm, points at something specific to those companies or that listing venue rather than at China's economy."
